       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for ibuprofen.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.\n- **Daily total:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use. 6,400 mg/day puts the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,600 mg total per day, split into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note. I'd recommend confirming with pharmacy first."
      }
