       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 1600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. At that dose the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events is high, and the extra dose adds toxicity without more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum:** for example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Enter a different analgesic plan:** if the pain isn't controlled at the maximum ibuprofen dose, add scheduled acetaminophen or another agent rather than raising the ibuprofen.\n- **Involve pharmacy:** if you think this patient has an unusual indication, a pharmacist or the attending can review it. The order can go in through whatever override process your hospital requires.\n\nIf you give me a different dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
